PALACE = {1: {'place': 'A science museum', 'intro': "Walk through a science museum, hall by hall. In each hall a strange exhibit hands you the module's core idea.", 'stations': [('1.1', 'Entrance hall', 'In the entrance hall a giant set of scales holds a stone tablet of equations on one side and a bucket of sparkling data beads on the other; a robot balances them with one finger and then walks off to drive a tiny car.'), ('1.2', 'Hall of change', 'In the hall of change a giant hourglass drains sand at a speed that slows as it empties; a child with a measuring stick hops along beside it, one hop per tick, sometimes overshooting so far she bounces off the wall.'), ('1.3', 'Hall of switches', 'In the hall of switches, rows of dimmer switches each glow softly from dark to bright as you walk past; a conductor waves a baton and their glows add up into the shape of a wave painted on the wall.'), ('1.4', 'Hall of hills', 'In the hall of hills a blindfolded skier feels the slope with her poles and takes steps downhill; one step too big and she flies over a ridge, but a heavy rolling snowball beside her ploughs straight through the small bumps into the deepest valley.'), ('1.5', 'Physics gallery', 'In the physics gallery a painter copies six dots onto a canvas, then a stern professor with a ruler walks along the rest of the canvas tapping it every few centimetres, and wherever he taps the line bends obediently into a perfect fading curve.'), ('1.6', 'Hall of mirrors', "In the hall of mirrors a tailor measures a statue covered in buzzing flies; one apprentice sews a stiff box that fits nothing, another sews a suit that copies every fly, and a quiet third sews to the statue's true shape while a judge holds up a fresh, fly-free statue to compare."), ('1.7', 'Hall of copies', "In the hall of copies, a huge slow clockwork machine grinds out one answer per hour onto cards; a quick child pins the few cards on a corkboard and stretches a rubber band through the pins, then answers visitors' questions instantly by reading the band."), ('1.8', 'Robot workshop', 'In the robot workshop a robot dog with a blindfold sniffs the air, guesses where its ball has rolled, then peeks once through a foggy window and leaps halfway between its guess and what it saw, landing right on the ball.')]}, 2: {'place': 'A workshop', 'intro': "Walk along the benches of a maker's workshop. At each bench a machine is half built; its odd scene holds the step you need.", 'stations': [('2.1', 'Front bench', "At the front bench a carpenter refuses to cut any wood until a sign reading THE QUESTION is nailed up; behind her a nosy apprentice tries to peek over a curtain at tomorrow's answers and is gently turned around to face yesterday."), ('2.2', 'Network bench', 'At the network bench a watchmaker assembles a little clockwork bird; she taps it at forty marked spots along a rail to check it obeys the fading rule, and a dial labelled k slowly turns itself from 0.3 to 0.8 as the bird starts to sing in tune.'), ('2.3', 'Grid bench', "At the grid bench a row of cooks pass a hot potato to their neighbours every second; when the head cook shouts 'faster!' past the half-mark, they start throwing it so hard it explodes into a shower of sparks over the workshop."), ('2.4', 'Detective bench', 'At the detective bench a sleuth lays seven suspects in a line labelled 1, x, v, x², xv, v², x³; she shines a lamp, and five of them fade away to nothing, leaving x and v holding up a sign that reads −4 and −0.3.'), ('2.5', 'Translator bench', "At the translator bench a machine with two hoppers swallows a whole painted landscape in one and a single coordinate card in the other, then instantly prints the temperature at that spot; a shelf of example paintings behind it is labelled 'only works for landscapes like these'."), ('2.6', 'Fog bench', "At the fog bench a sculptor pins a ribbon to a few posts; between nearby posts the fog around the ribbon is thin, between distant posts it billows thick, and an inspector with a stopwatch checks that the ribbon's true path stays inside the fog nineteen times out of twenty."), ('2.7', 'Repair bench', 'At the repair bench an old straight wooden ruler is laid along a curved road model; a small, patient apprentice glues thin slivers under it only where the road curves away, and beyond the end of the workbench the ruler still points the right way while a wild free-hand sketch next to it flies off the table.'), ('2.8', 'Shipping bench', "At the shipping bench every finished machine gets a luggage tag reading 'good for these roads, not those'; an inspector wraps each in a stretchy band that fits small boxes loosely and big boxes too tightly, while a red 'safe mode' lever waits by the door.")]}, 3: {'place': 'A city journey', 'intro': 'Ride across a city: motorway, junction, crossing, power station, climate office, stadium, control room and university. Each stop shows one application.', 'stations': [('3.1', 'Motorway bridge', "On the motorway bridge a few lighthouse keepers stand far apart shining lamps on the traffic; between them a ghostly river of light flows, bending and bunching exactly where the keepers' lamps say a jam has formed, while a child's straight chalk line on the bridge misses it completely."), ('3.2', 'Busy junction', 'At the busy junction a line of ten wind-up toy cars rolls past; when the first one hiccups, each one behind jerks harder until the last one falls over, but when they hold hands with glowing radio strings the hiccup fades to a gentle ripple.'), ('3.3', 'Pedestrian crossing', 'At the pedestrian crossing a giant stopwatch hangs over two cars nose to tail, counting down seconds to impact; near-miss confetti rains down in great heaps, while only a single sad crumpled hubcap lies at the very top of a tall pyramid of confetti.'), ('3.4', 'Power station', 'At the power station a car on a treadmill climbs a tilting ramp while four arm-wrestlers labelled INERTIA, HILL, TYRES and WIND pull it back; a tiny accountant beside it writes corrections into a ledger whenever the engine coughs differently than the chart predicts.'), ('3.5', 'Climate office', 'In the climate office a giant clockwork globe takes six hours to spin out each forecast card; a clerk pins five cards along a carbon-price rail, drapes a silk ribbon through them with fog where she is unsure, and sends the globe to spin next wherever the fog is thickest.'), ('3.6', 'Stadium gate', "At the stadium gate a speedometer on every fan's hat slows as the crowd thickens; a rubber-band curve stretched only over the quiet edge of the crowd flies up into the sky over the packed centre, while a sturdy brass rail bends gracefully down to zero exactly where people are packed shoulder to shoulder."), ('3.7', 'Control room', 'In the control room a glass model of the junction glows on a table; every ninety seconds a messenger runs in with a slip of paper and nudges the glass cars to match, and when the messenger falls asleep the glass cars keep moving on their own, just a little less sure.'), ('3.8', 'University gate', 'At the university gate five signposts point to unexplored valleys labelled FOUNDATION, WORLD, VERIFY, RARE and FAIR; a scribe at a lectern writes a report in which every number holds hands with a baseline and wears a little pair of brackets for its uncertainty.')]}}
